---
source: tests/cli/basics.rs
expression: text(&output.stdout)?
---
fetch something once, without a project

usage: fetchloom get [options] <link>

arguments:
  <link>  what to download: search words, a link, a DOI, or an id such as zenodo:3608990

options:
  -o, --output <dir>    put the download in <dir> instead of a new folder named after it
      --select <glob>   keep only files matching this pattern, such as "**/*.csv". repeat it for more
      --exclude <glob>  leave out files matching this pattern. repeat it for more
      --no-extract      keep zip and tar archives packed instead of unpacking them
  -q, --quiet           print only the answer and errors
  -v, --verbose...      say more: -v adds detail and counters, -vv adds debug logs
      --json            print one JSON document on stdout instead of the story
      --offline         use only what is already on this machine
  -y, --yes             approve confirmations, but never choose a dataset for you
      --color <when>    when to use color [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -C <dir>              run as if fetchloom started in <dir>
  -h, --help            print help

examples:
  fetchloom get iris
  fetchloom get zenodo:3608990
  fetchloom get zenodo:3608990 -o flowers
  fetchloom get https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mwaskom/seaborn-data/master/iris.csv

on disk: writes the output folder through the cache. does not create project files
